    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Larmer Property is delighted to introduce to the market the former Clones Dry Cleaners, an exceptional development and investment opportunity situated on Lower Fermanagh Street in the heart of Clones, Co. Monaghan. \r\n\r\nPositioned squarely in a prime town-centre location, this property offers immediate, walk-to access to all everyday shops, services, and local amenities.  Adding to its practical appeal, the rear of the property directly backs onto the SuperValu car park, offering superb convenience for access, parking, and town navigation.   \r\n\r\nSite Size:\r\n470 Sq. Metres / 0.116 Acres / 0.047 Hectares\r\n\r\nPlanning Permission & Potential Layout\r\nA standout feature of this listing is its completed change of use. Transitioning from its original footprint as a commercial dry cleaning business, the property now comes with full planning permission for conversion into a modern 2-bedroom residence.   This pre-approved planning removes significant bureaucratic delays and uncertainty for the incoming owner. \r\nWhether you are an investor looking to add a high-demand rental to your portfolio or a buyer seeking to build a custom town-centre residence, the layout provides a clear, actionable roadmap for transformation.\r\n\r\nModernisation Project & The €70,000 Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant\r\nThe property is currently in raw condition and requires full modernisation, including a complete re-wire, re-plumbing, structural updates, and comprehensive interior fit-out.   \r\nCrucially, because the building has been vacant and structurally disused for an extended period, it qualifies for the Derelict Property Refurbishment Grant of up to €70,000 (Under the Croí Cónaithe / Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant scheme).  \r\n\r\nKey Benefits of the Grant: \r\n\r\nDirect Equity Injection: Up to €70,000 in non-repayable grant funding significantly reduces the net out-of-pocket capital required for major works like re-wiring, re-plumbing, roofing, and structural repairs.\r\n\r\nImproved Energy Performance: Grant funds can be paired with additional SEAI energy efficiency grants (such as insulation, heat pumps, and window upgrades) to transform a historic structure into a high-BER rating modern home. \r\n\r\nBy offsetting heavy renovation costs through state support, investors and homebuilders can achieve a finished project value well above their total capital outlay.\r\n\r\nStrategic Location & Regional Connectivity\r\nClones is a historic market town experiencing significant local investment and renewal in the last number of years.  A major highlight for the area is the ongoing Ulster Canal restoration project.  This ambitious redevelopment is revitalising the waterway network through Clones, driving local tourism, improving recreational infrastructure, and creating a vibrant destination for both residents and visitors.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the property benefits immensely from its strategic border position. Located just minutes from the Northern Ireland border, Clones shares close proximity to neighbouring Northern Irish counties such as Fermanagh and Tyrone.  This seamless cross-border connectivity makes the location highly attractive for buyers or tenants commuting across the region for work, education, or leisure.\r\n\r\nAn Unmissable Investment:\r\nPriced competitively to sell, this property represents one of the most accessible entry points into the Co. Monaghan property market.  The combination of its central town-centre placement, the €70,000 derelict grant eligibility, full planning permission for a 2-bedroom home, and the broader economic resurgence driven by the Ulster Canal project makes this former Clones Dry Cleaners an unmissable prospect.   \r\n\r\nContact us today to arrange a viewing."
      },
